12: ## 1. Executive Summary & Verification Philosophy
13: 
14: Milestone 5 introduces the media playback engine and 10-foot On-Screen Display (OSD) controls for the Cinejoy webOS television application. Because webOS media playback depends on MediaSource Extensions (MSE), native HTML5 `<video>`, and external cryptographic streaming proxy services, verifying playback in headless CI or development workstations requires a deterministic simulation harness.
15: 
16: The verification harness (`app/test-m5.js` / `app/test-player.js`) is engineered with the following core principles:
17: 1. **100% Offline & Hermetic Execution**: Zero reliance on physical LG TV hardware, real display servers, live CDN endpoints (`lightspeed.st`), or external network traffic.
18: 2. **Complete Native Media Simulation**: Full deterministic mocking of `HTMLMediaElement` (`play`, `pause`, `load`, `currentTime`, `duration`, `buffered`, `readyState`, `seeking`, `timeupdate`, `ended`) and `window.Hls` (lifecycle, event pipeline, error types, bitrate quality levels, audio/subtitle tracks, resource destruction).
19: 3. **Six Distinct Verification Suites (46 Discrete Checks)**: Exceeds the >= 40 check threshold across all Milestone 5 feature vectors:
20:    - **Suite 1**: Stream Resolution & Ingestion (7 checks)
21:    - **Suite 2**: Player Lifecycle & State Management (8 checks)
22:    - **Suite 3**: 10-Foot TV OSD & Controls (8 checks)
23:    - **Suite 4**: Remote Control Keybindings (8 checks)
24:    - **Suite 5**: Subtitle & Server Switching (7 checks)
25:    - **Suite 6**: Buffering, Errors & Resume Tracking (8 checks)
26: 4. **Deterministic Time Control**: Virtualized clock manipulation for the 4000ms OSD auto-hide timer, 15000ms stream stall watchdog, and debounced seek updates without flaky real-world timeouts.
27: 5. **Zero Regressions Semantics**: Exit code `0` on 100% pass, non-zero on any failure, maintaining zero regressions against the cumulative 308 automated checks from Milestones 1–4.
